    feat(board): first-class deferred task flag (BT-076)
    
    A task row may carry a boolean `deferred` field, distinct from blocked and
    complete: deferral is "the owner parked this on purpose", not "something is
    wrong" and not "this is done". Deferred rows stay searchable and retained in
    list/show/export/import; what changes is reporting — they are counted
    separately and excluded from the pending/actionable tally, so a board whose
    only open row is deferred no longer reads as having pending work (Bane
    2026-10-05: deferred work must not wake a tasks-admission foreman).
    
    - keys.go: `deferred` joins the sanctioned task-row key canon (create's
      schema mirroring and validate must never flag it as drift).
    - read.go: RowIsDeferred reads the raw bytes (true/True literals only;
      null/absent/false — and any non-boolean, which validate warns about —
      read as NOT deferred, mirroring priorityLabel's style). Stats grows
      `deferred` + `actionable` JSON keys; RenderText prints both lines;
      ComputeStats keeps deferred rows in Total and in the by-status tally but
      excludes them from Actionable (actionable = non-deferred pending rows).
    - write.go: TaskRowSpec.Deferred / UpdateSpec.Deferred (*bool, the BT-037
      nil-untouched discipline). create --deferred writes deferred:true; an
      omitted flag writes NO key — create never neutral-mirrors the key from
      the last row (a deferred:true board would otherwise stamp
      deferred:null on every fresh row; RED-proven: disabling the skip fails
      both the board-level and CLI omitted-flag tests with that exact shape).
      update --deferred false writes deferred:false (never deletes the key);
      an omitted update leaves the key untouched; --deferred joins the
      change-flag gate and --normalize's refusal list.
    - validate.go: a non-boolean deferred value is an itemized WARNING (board
      stays exit-0), same soft-field convention as priority/depends_on shape
      drift; absent/true/false/null stay silent.
    - cmd/boardctl: `create --deferred` (bare bool flag, excluded from
      reorderArgs value flags) and `update --deferred true|false`
      (strconv.ParseBool; a non-boolean spelling is a usage error with nothing
      written). Both usage closures and the root usageText document the flags
      (usage-closure meta-tests stay green). stats/umbrella output carries the
      separate deferred + actionable lines; umbrella aggregates both.
    - internal/render: Derived.deferred_count counts deferred rows; open_count
      excludes them (the actionable reading behind completion % and the
      burndown headline); complete rows that are deferred still count complete.
    - README: "The deferred flag (BT-076)" subsection under the task-field docs.
    
    Tests: bt076_deferred_test.go (board-level write contract, canon
    sanctioning, validate warning, stats split, list/show retention, BT-022
    raw-import verbatim round-trip), bt076_cli_test.go (create/update flags,
    invalid-value usage error, help closure, stats text+JSON),
    bt076_deferred_derive_test.go (deferred_count/open_count/complete split).
    
    Suite: go build ./... && go vet ./... && gofmt -l (clean) && go test
    ./... -count=1 — all packages ok. Live CLI probe on a scratch board:
    create --deferred / update --deferred false / stats / stats --json /
    validate all behave per contract.
    
    ch:trace row=BT-076 evidence=go test ./... -count=1 green + RED-proof on
    the create mirror-skip + commit (this commit)
